  <layout>One block of text on one printed page: a title block at the top in capitals and italics, then a verse poem in one column with a woodcut initial at its left, ending with a catchword "SYL-" at the lower right. No margin notes, no running head, no page number.</layout>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">PAVLI</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="1">MELISSI FRANCI,</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="1">COMITIS PAL. EQVITIS AVR.</l>
    <l n="4" type="heading" level="1">ET CIVIS ROMANI, CONSILIARII</l>
    <l n="5" type="heading" level="1">Archipalatini,</l>
    <l n="6" type="heading" level="1">MELOS</l>
    <l n="7" type="heading" level="1">AD MELIOREM HAIMINSFELDIVM</l>
    <l n="8" type="heading" level="1">GOLDASTVM, Nobilem HELVETIVM.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">VIC QVID abstrufo latet in recessu</l>
    <l n="10">Sæculi GOLDASTE vetustioris,</l>
    <l n="11">Eruis vulgans, &amp; apertiores</l>
    <l n="12">Mittis in auras.</l>
    <l n="13">Additis sollerte notis Minervâ.</l>
    <l n="14">Digna nimirum &amp; pretiosa gaza</l>
    <l n="15">Sunt libri, quos cura vigil sagaxq;</l>
    <l n="16">Cœnobiorum</l>
    <l n="17">Præstitit sartos hodieque tectos.</l>
    <l n="18">FVLDA cum primis celebranda Francis,</l>
    <l n="19">Deinde LAVRISSÆ domus ad beati</l>
    <l n="20">Flumina Rheni,</l>
    <l n="21">Integri custos veneranda LivI,</l>
    <l n="22">Nescio quo furetagace rapti.</l>
    <l n="23">Addé CORBEIÆ pluteos, sacrique</l>
    <l n="24">Pulpita GALLI,</l>
    <l n="25">Quæ tuus SCHOBINGER adire tuto,</l>
    <l n="26">Tuque item quisti, studiose prisci</l>
    <l n="27">Temporis, rarâque adeo repertu</l>
    <l n="28">(Quorsus catur)</l>
    <l n="29">Paginæ, quâ sestilus HVNIBALDI</l>
    <l n="30">Prodidit, Reges veterum recensens</l>
    <l n="31">Resque Francorum; licet ipse nugax</l>
    <l n="32">Audiat auctor.</l>
    <l n="33">Pluribus, queis nec tamen eius vmquam</l>
    <l n="34">Scripta sint visa, aut aliquando lecta.</l>
    <l n="35">Momon in tantum cacoëthes vrget</l>
    <l n="36">Stare cauillis.</l>
    <l n="37">Tu viâ cœptâ MELIOR secundis</l>
    <l n="38">Perge sis astris, nitidiq; ductum</l>
    <l n="39">LECTII prono sequere æmulatu,</l>
    <l n="40">Aureæ Graii.</l>
    <l n="41">Oris adsertor, Latiæq; linguæ;</l>
    <l n="42">Excitus Famæ monitis, parentis</l>
    <l n="43">Inter æquævos tibi Principatum,</l>
    <l n="44">Ditequeregnum.</l>
    <l n="45" para="true">SYL-</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The woodcut initial "V" at the start of the first verse line is a decorative ornamental block; read as "VIC QVID". The catchword "SYL-" is at lower right. Some words in the verse are set in spaced capitals and small capitals; ornament at the left of the first stanza is a woodcut frame, not text.</notes>
</page>
